  "narrative": [
    {
      "text": "Fiber Functors of Equivariantizations of Finite Tensor Categories — Let G be a finite group acting on a finite tensor category C.\n\n**Fiber Functors of Equivariantizations of Finite Tensor Categories**\n\n*CÉSAR GALINDO, CLAUDIA GALLEGO, AND YIBY MORALES*\n\n34 pp, 16 sections.\n\n**Abstract.** Let G be a finite group acting on a finite tensor category C. We classify fiber functors on the equivariantization CG in terms of equivariant exact module categories over C, indexed by subgroups of G. The data are a subgroup H ⊆G and an H-equivariant C-module category M whose underlying C-module category is indecomposable, exact, and semisimple; they give a fiber functor precisely when H acts transitively on the simple objects of M and the stabilizer cocycle of one, hence every, simple object is non-degenerate. Through Tannaka–Krein reconstruction this describes realizations of CG as the representation category of a finite-dimensional Hopf algebra, with no semisimplicity hypothesis on C.\n\n**Outline.** Front matter; 1 Introduction; 2.2 Equivariant tensor categories and their mo; 2 Preliminaries; 2.1 Finite tensor categories and their module ; 2.3 The equivariant category CG and its module; 3 Fiber functors for CG; 3.1 The correspondence between fiber functors ; 3.2 Rank-one equivariantizations; 3.3 Classification of fiber functors; 4 Fiber functors for the Hopf algebras Hp; 4.1 Tambara–Yamagami categories and fiber func; 4.3 Classification of fiber functors for Rep(H; 5 Fiber functors on gaugings; 5.1 First reductions for small radical gauging; References",
